  "description": "Array of 7 NPN Darlington pairs with high-voltage open-collector outputs and common-cathode freewheeling clamp diodes brought out to the COM pin. Each channel has a 2.7k series base resistor so inputs drive directly from TTL or 5V CMOS logic. Each output sinks up to 500mA at outputs rated to 50V, switching relays, solenoids, steppers and lamps from logic-level control. Widely used on 28BYJ-48 stepper driver boards and relay boards.",
